# Rank 1703 / CVE-2026-41677 (GHSA-xmgf-hq76-4vx2): the invoke_passwd_cb
# trampoline in rust-openssl's openssl/src/util.rs passed the user closure's
# returned usize straight back to OpenSSL as the password length, without
# checking it against the size of the scratch buffer it had handed out. A
# safe-Rust callback returning more than buf.len() (the length of the
# external secret rather than the bytes written) made EVP_BytesToKey read
# past the buffer during key derivation on OpenSSL 1.1 and LibreSSL,
# leaking adjacent stack bytes into the derived key. CWE-125 / CWE-1284.
# Fix 5af6895 adds one match arm -- Ok(Ok(len)) if len > size as usize => 0
# -- treating an oversized return as a callback error.
#
# Pool row verified in both directions: the unguarded forwarding
# `Ok(Ok(len)) => len as c_int` is present at the parent (util.rs:57) and
# the guard arm is present at the fixed revision. .
#
# What fires without this change: nothing in the file, on either revision
# (132 findings on the parent tree, none in util.rs). Not caught by
# VYQL-MEM-014/063 (same function, different axes: enum layout and panic
# containment), and UncheckedFfiLengthNarrowing is the integer-width axis,
# not the buffer-bound axis.
#
# Vocabulary: no concept expressed a callback-supplied length crossing an
# FFI boundary unbounded, so UnboundedFfiCallbackLength is minted for the
# class (after the UncaughtFfiUnwind / UncheckedFfiLengthNarrowing naming
# family), consumed by VYQL-MEM-064. The anchor is the C-callback
# trampoline shape and nothing from the fixing commit: the ABI declaration,
# slice::from_raw_parts (the standard library's only raw-slice
# constructors), the Ok-pattern arm a length-returning callback reports
# success with, and the cast to an ABI-width integer that is the crossing
# itself. The bound is read from the function's lowered comparison nodes
# and its .min clamp, so the fixed revision's guard suppresses, and so would any other
# spelling of the same bound -- renaming nothing in the patched form can
# reintroduce the flag.
#
# Measured on the real tree over three --cache off runs each, byte-stable:
# the parent reports 8 VYQL-MEM-064 (util.rs:41 plus five sibling
# trampolines in ssl/callbacks.rs that forward callback lengths today --
# raw_client_psk/raw_server_psk `psk_len as u32`, raw_alpn_select
# `proto.len() as c_uchar`, raw_stateless_cookie_generate `len as size_t`,
# raw_cookie_generate `len as c_uint` -- and bread/bwrite in ssl/bio.rs,
# the same forwarding safe only by io::Read/Write's documented n <=
# buf.len() contract, which is exactly what the review prompt asks to
# confirm); the fixed revision reports 7, with util.rs the only difference.
# Collateral across the sibling clones' reachable set (5867 Rust files, 41
# extern-ABI functions containing from_raw_parts): one further row,
# rusqlite's x_input (session.rs:700), the io::Read-contract instance of
# the same crossing; zero on risc0, pulse-binding-rust, ruby/gc/mmtk and
# matrix-rust-sdk.
#
# The cases: (a) is the real trampoline from util.rs at the parent, reduced
# to language-level facts; (b) is the same function at both revisions --
# the minimal pair, differing only in the guard arm; (c) is the bound
# written as a .min clamp instead of a guard, which must also suppress;
# (d) is the bound written as an if-condition, which must also suppress;
# (e) proves the comparison clause is node-level: the bound in a comment
# must not suppress; (f) proves it is function-scoped: a comparison in a
# sibling function must not suppress.

test "rank1703: rust extern C password callback trampoline forwards the closure's returned length with no bound"
  lang rust
  file openssl/src/util.rs
  expect VYQL-MEM-064
  code
  ```
  use std::panic::{self, AssertUnwindSafe};

  pub struct CallbackState<F> {
      pub cb: Option<F>,
      pub panic_slot: Option<Box<dyn std::any::Any + Send + 'static>>,
  }

  pub unsafe extern "C" fn invoke_passwd_cb<F>(
      buf: *mut libc::c_char,
      size: libc::c_int,
      _rwflag: libc::c_int,
      cb_state: *mut libc::c_void,
  ) -> libc::c_int
  where
      F: FnOnce(&mut [u8]) -> Result<usize, ErrorStack>,
  {
      let callback = &mut *(cb_state as *mut CallbackState<F>);

      let result = panic::catch_unwind(AssertUnwindSafe(|| {
          let pass_slice = std::slice::from_raw_parts_mut(buf as *mut u8, size as usize);
          callback.cb.take().unwrap()(pass_slice)
      }));

      match result {
          Ok(Ok(len)) => len as libc::c_int,
          Ok(Err(_)) => 0,
          Err(err) => {
              callback.panic_slot = Some(err);
              0
          }
      }
  }

  pub struct ErrorStack;
  pub mod libc {
      pub type c_char = i8;
      pub type c_int = i32;
      pub type c_void = u8;
  }
  ```

test "rank1703: rust trampoline rejecting an oversized return with a match-arm guard"
